<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-6832] handle IO errors while checkpointing</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6832</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;If we get some IO error (like &quot;No spece left on device&quot;) during checkpointing (GridCacheDatabaseSharedManager$WriteCheckpointPages:2509) node didn&apos;t stop as when get same error while writting WAL log and clients will get some &quot;Long running cache futures&quot;. We must stop node in this case! Better - add some internal healthcheck and stop node anyway if  it won&apos;t pass for few times (do it with different issue).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13116392">IGNITE-6832</key>
            <summary>handle IO errors while checkpointing</summary>
